Week 2026-W42: 5 releases, 1 needs action

One Ollama fix needs action this week; the rest can wait.

🔴 Act now

- Ollama v0.13.0
  What changed: Fixes a crash when a model is larger than the available VRAM.
  What to do: Upgrade before the next scheduled run.
  https://github.com/ollama/ollama/releases/tag/v0.13.0

🟡 Worth a look

- Docker Desktop 4.50 & Compose 2.40
  What changed: Compose watch now rebuilds only the services whose files changed.
  Relevant if you: develop with Compose watch.
  https://docs.docker.com/desktop/release-notes/

- vLLM v0.11.2
  What changed: Drops support for Node < 20 tooling and adds a prefix-cache metric.
  Relevant if you: serve models with vLLM.
  https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/releases/tag/v0.11.2

⚪ Good to know

- LangGraph 1.1
  What changed: Adds typed checkpoints for long-running graphs.
  https://github.com/langchain-ai/langgraph/releases/tag/1.1.0

- Node.js 24.11.0
  What changed: Routine LTS update with security fixes already shipped last week.
  https://nodejs.org/en/blog/release/v24.11.0

Guards off this run: input guard.
